= Statistical Modelling

This stage of the project will investigate the statistical structure of the learned embedding space and the significance of distances between embeddings.

Covariance-based approaches, such as Mahalanobis distance, will be investigated to model normal regions within the embedding space. The resulting ellipsoidal regions may provide a more interpretable representation of normal behaviour and anomaly detection compared to simple distance-based approaches. Rather than using a fixed-radius threshold, ellipsoidal modelling adapts the boundary of normal behaviour to the underlying data distribution, allowing variation to be represented differently along each principal direction.

The statistical structure of the embedding space will also be analysed using image metadata, such as object category and defect type, to investigate whether different anomalies form distinct regions or patterns within it.
